    {
      "key": "seed_genes",
      "value_json": "[{\"type\":\"formulation\",\"text\":\"Separate block masses from within-block mass fractions at block sizes 2, 4, 8, and 16. Hold block masses fixed initially and optimize nonnegative fractions from randomized asymmetric starts, then release both scales jointly. Test finite departures from uniform fractions, not only infinitesimal steps. Preserve the incumbent and compare endpoints using the exact verifier.\"},{\"type\":\"structure\",\"text\":\"Choose hybridization parents by structural distance as well as score. Normalize mass, account for translation and reflection equivalences, and compare coarse mass profiles and support masks. Reject numerically identical parent pairs. Recombine complementary spatial regions with several boundary choices, then jointly refit regional weights and amplitudes before exact endpoint comparison.\"},{\"type\":\"structure\",\"text\":\"Launch independent coarse-grid searches without inheriting the incumbent support. Retain structurally distinct solutions even when their coarse scores are lower. Lift several finalists through increasing resolutions using mass-preserving resampling and amplitude optimization, never exceeding two million cells. Judge success only after full-resolution exact rescoring, keeping the original incumbent separately.\"}]"
    }
  ]
